# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
# Export real cookies from your browser — DO NOT commit this file with real values.
#
# How to create cookies.txt for AWS EC2:
# 1. Install "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" browser extension
# 2. Open YouTube in a private/incognito window and sign in
# 3. Export cookies for youtube.com → save as cookies.txt
# 4. scp cookies.txt to EC2: ~/ytnotesmaker/cookies.txt
# 5. docker compose restart backend
#
# Replace this file with your exported cookies (first line must be the Netscape header below):

# .youtube.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	0	PLACEHOLDER	name=value
